From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] DVDVideoCodecAmlogic: MJPEG is decoded in software

A cut of a film kept its cover picture, a 3840x2160 JPEG, as a second
video track of a single frame. Playing it, the hardware MJPEG decoder
was created for that track and the S6 locked up at once: no panic
message, no trace, a reset by the watchdog.

MJPEG is no longer opened on the hardware decoder, so Kodi decodes it
with FFmpeg, as it does on every other platform: a cover picture or a
camera clip costs little to decode in software, and no file can take
the box down through it.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecAmlogic.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecAmlogic.cpp
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecAmlogic.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecAmlogic.cpp
@@ -157,8 +157,8 @@
   switch(m_hints.codec)
   {
     case AV_CODEC_ID_MJPEG:
-      m_pFormatName = "am-mjpeg";
-      break;
+      // decoded in software: the hardware locked the chip on a 4K picture
+      goto FAIL;
     case AV_CODEC_ID_MPEG1VIDEO:
     case AV_CODEC_ID_MPEG2VIDEO:
       if (m_hints.width <= CServiceBroker::GetSettingsComponent()->GetSettings()->GetInt(CSettings::SETTING_VIDEOPLAYER_USEAMCODECMPEG2))
